IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`

-- ccc20-part16-taking-before-justice.l4 -- section 503 of the Criminal Code (Canada): taking the arrested person before a justice. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text; nothing is claimed verified against the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); a duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE.
-- HOURS: the core's Length of time has years, months and days only, so the 24 hours of paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) are a plain NUMBER of hours (NEEDS-CORE.md); the six days of (3)(b)(i) are a NUMBER of days.
-- This module imports `ccc-definitions` for `s 2 justice`: "a justice" in this section means what section 2 says, so the person the accused was taken before is described by `s 2 justice kind`.

§ `Section 503(1) and (2) -- Taking before a justice`

-- src:11201 | Taking before justice
-- src:11202 | 503 (1) Subject to the other provisions of this section, a peace officer who arrests a person with or without warrant and who has not released the person under any other provision under this Part or under section 705.1 shall, in accordance with the following paragraphs, cause the person to be taken before a justice to be dealt with according to law:
-- src:11203 | (a) if a justice is available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested by the peace officer, the person shall be taken before a justice without unreasonable delay and in any event within that period; and
-- src:11204 | (b) if a justice is not available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested by the peace officer, the person shall be taken before a justice as soon as possible.
@ref s 503(1) (src:11201-11204)
GIVEN `the peace officer arrested the person, with or without warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer has released the person under another provision of this Part or under section 705.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(1) the peace officer must cause the person to be taken before a justice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the peace officer arrested the person, with or without warrant` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a peace officer who arrests a person with or without warrant"
        IF `the peace officer has released the person under another provision of this Part or under section 705.1` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and who has not released the person under any other provision under this Part or under section 705.1"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Whether the person was taken before a justice in time. (a) a justice is available within 24 hours of the arrest: without unreasonable delay and in any event within that period. (b) no justice is
-- available within 24 hours: as soon as possible. The hours are counted as `s 503(2)` says. Exactly 24 hours is within the period.
@ref s 503(1)(a) and (b) (src:11203-11204)
GIVEN `a justice is available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours between the start of the period and the person being taken before a justice` IS A NUMBER
      `the person was taken before a justice without unreasonable delay` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was taken before a justice as soon as possible` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(1) the person was taken before a justice as paragraph (a) or (b) requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a justice is available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested` AND NOT `the person was taken before a justice without unreasonable delay`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) ... the person shall be taken before a justice without unreasonable delay"
        IF `a justice is available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested` AND `the hours between the start of the period and the person being taken before a justice` GREATER THAN 24
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and in any event within that period" (a period of 24 hours)
        IF `a justice is available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the person was taken before a justice as soon as possible` THEN JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) if a justice is not available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested by the peace officer, the person shall be taken before a justice as soon as possible"

-- The duty as a regulative rule, on the file's clock of HOURS after the start of the period. Where a justice is available within 24 hours the officer must take the person within 24 hours; otherwise
-- as soon as possible, which states no number, so that rule has no WITHIN. (The core's Party has `a peace officer` and `a justice`; the act is a local constructor.)
@ref s 503(1) the duty as a regulative rule (src:11201-11204)
DECLARE `s 503(1) the act` IS ONE OF
    `s 503(1) take the person before a justice`

@ref s 503(1) the duty as a regulative rule (src:11201-11204)
GIVEN `the answer of s 503(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a justice is available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 503(1) the act`
`s 503(1) the duty to take the person before a justice` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 503(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN IF `a justice is available within a period of 24 hours after the person has been arrested`
         THEN PARTY `a peace officer`
              MUST `s 503(1) take the person before a justice`
              WITHIN 24
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY `a peace officer` BECAUSE "the person was not taken before a justice within 24 hours after the arrest"
         ELSE PARTY `a peace officer`
              MUST `s 503(1) take the person before a justice`
              HENCE FULFILLED
              LEST BREACH BY `a peace officer` BECAUSE "the person was not taken before a justice as soon as possible"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The person the accused is taken before must be "a justice": section 2 says what that is (`s 2 justice` of ccc-definitions.l4).
@ref s 503(1) "a justice" is as section 2 defines it (src:11202)
GIVEN `the kind of judicial officer the person was taken before` IS A `s 2 justice kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(1) the person was taken before a justice within the meaning of section 2` MEANS
    `s 2 justice` `the kind of judicial officer the person was taken before`

-- src:11205 | Re-evaluation of detention
-- src:11206 | (1.1) At any time before the expiry of the time referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), a peace officer who is satisfied that the continued detention of the person in custody for an offence that is not listed in section 469 is no longer necessary shall release the person, if
-- src:11207 | (a) the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person; or
-- src:11208 | (b) the person gives an undertaking to the peace officer.
@ref s 503(1.1) (src:11205-11208)
GIVEN `the time referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) has not yet expired` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer is satisfied that the continued detention of the person in custody is no longer necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person gives an undertaking to the peace officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(1.1) the peace officer must release the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the time referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) has not yet expired` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At any time before the expiry of the time referred to in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)"
        IF NOT `the peace officer is satisfied that the continued detention of the person in custody is no longer necessary` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a peace officer who is satisfied that the continued detention of the person in custody ... is no longer necessary shall release the person"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "for an offence that is not listed in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for an offence that is not listed in section 469"
        IF `the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person` OR `the person gives an undertaking to the peace officer` THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a) or (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall release the person, if (a) the peace officer issues an appearance notice to the person; or (b) the person gives an undertaking to the peace officer"

-- 503 (2) Subsections (1) and (1.1) also apply to a peace officer to whom a person is delivered under subsection 494(3) or into whose custody a person is placed under subsection 163.5(3) of the Customs Act,
-- except that the 24-hour period referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) begins after the person is delivered to the officer. The function counts the hours that run against the period.
-- src:11209 | Person delivered or in custody
-- src:11210 | (2) Subsections (1) and (1.1) also apply to a peace officer to whom a person is delivered under subsection 494(3) or into whose custody a person is placed under subsection 163.5(3) of the Customs Act, except that the 24-hour period referred to in paragraphs (1)(a) and (b) begins after the person is delivered to the officer.
@ref s 503(2) (src:11209-11210)
GIVEN `the person was delivered to the officer under subsection 494(3) or placed in the officer's custody under subsection 163.5(3) of the Customs Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the hours since the arrest` IS A NUMBER
      `the hours since the person was delivered to the officer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 503(2) the hours that run against the 24-hour period` MEANS
    IF `the person was delivered to the officer under subsection 494(3) or placed in the officer's custody under subsection 163.5(3) of the Customs Act`
    THEN `the hours since the person was delivered to the officer`
    ELSE `the hours since the arrest`

§ `Section 503(3) and (3.1) -- Remand for return to the jurisdiction where the offence is alleged`

-- src:11214 | Remand in custody for return to jurisdiction where offence alleged to have been committed
-- src:11215 | (3) Where a person has been arrested without warrant for an indictable offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the territorial division where the arrest took place, the person shall, within the time prescribed in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), be taken before a justice within whose jurisdiction the person was arrested unless, where the offence was alleged to have been committed within the province in which the person was arrested, the person was taken before a justice within whose jurisdiction the offence was alleged to have been committed, and the justice within whose jurisdiction the person was arrested
-- src:11216 | (a) if the justice is not satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person arrested is the person alleged to have committed the offence, shall release that person; or
-- src:11217 | (b) if the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person arrested is the person alleged to have committed the offence, may
-- src:11218 | (i) remand the person to the custody of a peace officer to await execution of a warrant for his or her arrest in accordance with section 528, but if no warrant is so executed within a period of six days after the time he or she is remanded to such custody, the person in whose custody he or she then is shall release him or her, or
-- src:11219 | (ii) where the offence was alleged to have been committed within the province in which the person was arrested, order the person to be taken before a justice having jurisdiction with respect to the offence.
@ref s 503(3) (src:11214-11219)
DECLARE `s 503(3) the case` HAS
    `the person has been arrested without warrant for an indictable offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the territorial division where the arrest took place` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the offence was alleged to have been committed within the province in which the person was arrested` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person was taken before a justice within whose jurisdiction the offence was alleged to have been committed` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref s 503(3) the opening words (src:11214-11215)
GIVEN case IS A `s 503(3) the case`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(3) the person must, within the time prescribed in paragraph (1)(a) or (b), be taken before a justice within whose jurisdiction the person was arrested` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT case's `the person has been arrested without warrant for an indictable offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the territorial division where the arrest took place`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person has been arrested without warrant for an indictable offence alleged to have been committed in Canada outside the territorial division where the arrest took place"
        IF case's `the offence was alleged to have been committed within the province in which the person was arrested` AND case's `the person was taken before a justice within whose jurisdiction the offence was alleged to have been committed`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, where the offence was alleged to have been committed within the province in which the person was arrested, the person was taken before a justice within whose jurisdiction the offence was alleged to have been committed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 503(3)(a) (src:11216)
GIVEN `the arrest case of subsection (3) applies and the person is before the justice within whose jurisdiction the person was arrested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person arrested is the person alleged to have committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(3)(a) the justice must release the person` MEANS
    IF `the arrest case of subsection (3) applies and the person is before the justice within whose jurisdiction the person was arrested` AND NOT `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person arrested is the person alleged to have committed the offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the justice is not satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person arrested is the person alleged to have committed the offence, shall release that person"

DECLARE `s 503(3)(b) what the justice does` IS ONE OF
    `s 503(3)(b)(i) remand the person to the custody of a peace officer to await execution of a warrant in accordance with section 528`
    `s 503(3)(b)(ii) order the person to be taken before a justice having jurisdiction with respect to the offence`

@ref s 503(3)(b) (src:11217-11219)
GIVEN `the arrest case of subsection (3) applies and the person is before the justice within whose jurisdiction the person was arrested` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person arrested is the person alleged to have committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence was alleged to have been committed within the province in which the person was arrested` IS A BOOLEAN
      action IS A `s 503(3)(b) what the justice does`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(3)(b) the justice may take that step` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the arrest case of subsection (3) applies and the person is before the justice within whose jurisdiction the person was arrested` AND `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person arrested is the person alleged to have committed the offence`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) if the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds to believe that the person arrested is the person alleged to have committed the offence, may" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails)
        IF action EQUALS `s 503(3)(b)(ii) order the person to be taken before a justice having jurisdiction with respect to the offence` AND NOT `the offence was alleged to have been committed within the province in which the person was arrested`
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(ii) where the offence was alleged to have been committed within the province in which the person was arrested, order the person to be taken before a justice having jurisdiction with respect to the offence" (a "where" gate on a "may": the periods ruling (b) says JUST FALSE; the other reading is NOTHING; name-test sweep, listed)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 503(3)(b)(i) (src:11218)
GIVEN `the person was remanded under subparagraph (3)(b)(i)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a warrant was executed within a period of six days after the time of the remand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days since the remand` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(3)(b)(i) the person in whose custody the person then is must release them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person was remanded under subparagraph (3)(b)(i)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(i) remand the person to the custody of a peace officer to await execution of a warrant for his or her arrest in accordance with section 528, but if no warrant is so executed"
        IF `a warrant was executed within a period of six days after the time of the remand` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "but if no warrant is so executed within a period of six days after the time he or she is remanded to such custody"
        IF `the days since the remand` AT LEAST 6 THEN JUST TRUE   -- the period of six days has run: the release duty arises
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within a period of six days after the time he or she is remanded to such custody" (the six days have not yet run)

-- src:11220 | Interim release
-- src:11221 | (3.1) Notwithstanding paragraph (3)(b), a justice may, with the consent of the prosecutor, order that the person referred to in subsection (3), pending the execution of a warrant for the arrest of that person, be released
-- src:11222 | (a) without conditions; or
-- src:11223 | (b) on the terms of a release order containing any conditions referred to in paragraphs 515(2)(a) to (e) that the justice considers desirable and to which the prosecutor consents.
@ref s 503(3.1) (src:11220-11223)
DECLARE `s 503(3.1) the release ordered` IS ONE OF
    `s 503(3.1)(a) released without conditions`
    `s 503(3.1)(b) released on the terms of a release order containing conditions referred to in paragraphs 515(2)(a) to (e) that the justice considers desirable and to which the prosecutor consents`

@ref s 503(3.1) (src:11221-11223)
GIVEN `the person is one referred to in subsection (3), pending the execution of a warrant for their arrest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor consents to the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      release IS A `s 503(3.1) the release ordered`
      `the conditions are ones referred to in paragraphs 515(2)(a) to (e) that the justice considers desirable and to which the prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(3.1) the justice may order the person released` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is one referred to in subsection (3), pending the execution of a warrant for their arrest` AND `the prosecutor consents to the order`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a justice may, with the consent of the prosecutor, order that the person referred to in subsection (3), pending the execution of a warrant for the arrest of that person, be released" (a "may" whose gate fails)
        IF release EQUALS `s 503(3.1)(b) released on the terms of a release order containing conditions referred to in paragraphs 515(2)(a) to (e) that the justice considers desirable and to which the prosecutor consents`
           AND NOT `the conditions are ones referred to in paragraphs 515(2)(a) to (e) that the justice considers desirable and to which the prosecutor consents`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) on the terms of a release order containing any conditions referred to in paragraphs 515(2)(a) to (e) that the justice considers desirable and to which the prosecutor consents" (a "may" whose condition fails)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 503(4) and (5) -- Release of a person about to commit an indictable offence`

-- src:11224 | Release of person about to commit indictable offence
-- src:11225 | (4) A peace officer having the custody of a person who has been arrested without warrant as a person about to commit an indictable offence shall release that person as soon as practicable after the officer is satisfied that the continued detention of that person is no longer necessary in order to prevent that person from committing an indictable offence.
@ref s 503(4) (src:11224-11225)
GIVEN `the peace officer has custody of a person arrested without warrant as a person about to commit an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer is satisfied that the continued detention of that person is no longer necessary in order to prevent that person from committing an indictable offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(4) the peace officer must release the person as soon as practicable` MEANS
    IF `the peace officer has custody of a person arrested without warrant as a person about to commit an indictable offence`
       AND `the officer is satisfied that the continued detention of that person is no longer necessary in order to prevent that person from committing an indictable offence`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall release that person as soon as practicable after the officer is satisfied that the continued detention of that person is no longer necessary"

-- src:11226 | Consequences of non-release
-- src:11227 | (5) Despite subsection (4), a peace officer having the custody of a person referred to in that subsection who does not release the person before the expiry of the time prescribed in paragraph (1)(a) or (b) for taking the person before the justice shall be deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of the peace officer’s duty for the purposes of
-- src:11228 | (a) any proceedings under this or any other Act of Parliament; or
-- src:11229 | (b) any other proceedings, unless in those proceedings it is alleged and established by the person making the allegation that the peace officer did not comply with the requirements of subsection (4).
@ref s 503(5) (src:11226-11229)
GIVEN `the peace officer has custody of a person referred to in subsection (4) and did not release the person before the expiry of the time prescribed in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are under this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is alleged and established by the person making the allegation that the peace officer did not comply with subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 503(5) the peace officer is deemed to be acting lawfully and in the execution of the peace officer's duty` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the peace officer has custody of a person referred to in subsection (4) and did not release the person before the expiry of the time prescribed in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a peace officer having the custody of a person referred to in that subsection who does not release the person before the expiry of the time prescribed in paragraph (1)(a) or (b)"
        IF `the proceedings are under this or any other Act of Parliament` THEN JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (a): no exception is stated
        IF `it is alleged and established by the person making the allegation that the peace officer did not comply with subsection (4)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) any other proceedings, unless in those proceedings it is alleged and established by the person making the allegation"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- paragraph (b)
